// stdlib/ucase.sa -- full Unicode casing (prefix `uc_`).
//
// Dependency: import stdlib/utf8.sa BEFORE this module. Like money.sa over
// decimal.sa, this module names its dependency's functions without importing
// it, because the module loader does not dedupe a diamond and a second import
// would declare every u8_ function twice.
//
// What this is. The Unicode default case conversion of the UCD, not the ASCII
// one stdlib/utext.sa has: uc_upper, uc_lower and uc_title map one code point
// to as many as three, which is what makes "ß" uppercase to "SS", the "ﬁ"
// ligature to "FI" and a Greek iota-subscript form to two code points.
// uc_fold is Unicode default case folding, the recipe for caseless comparison:
// "Straße" and "STRASSE" fold to the same bytes. uc_cased and
// uc_case_ignorable answer the two UAX #44 properties that comparison needs,
// and uc_fold_equal applies all four.
//
// What this is not. There is no locale tailoring: the sixteen conditional
// SpecialCasing entries (Turkish/Azeri dot rules, Final_Sigma, Lithuanian and
// Dutch ij) are not modelled, so uc_upper("i") is "I" everywhere and
// UC_LOWER("Σ") is "σ" even at the end of a word. There is no NFKC_Casefold,
// no language-sensitive sentence titlecasing and no CLDR data at all.
// Compatibility folding is a separate job: call uc_fold and then un_nfc or
// un_nfd from stdlib/unorm.sa.
//
// Failure contract, the same as the rest of the text layer: a text function
// returns "" for malformed or over-long input, and a predicate -1. The list
// API returns [] when any element is not a scalar. A Sayanox string is a C
// string, so U+0000 can travel in a list but never in a string.
//
// The tables below are generated from the Unicode 17.0.0 Character Database
// files themselves (UnicodeData.txt for the simple one-code-point mappings,
// SpecialCasing.txt for the multi-code-point ones, CaseFolding.txt for the
// folds); see the marker comment.

// Cap shared with stdlib/utf8.sa: a wider input is refused, not truncated.
make uc_max_bytes() -> num {
  give 65536
}

// Bisection over a flat [lo, hi, ...] group table: the index of the group
// holding cp, or -1. The stride is a parameter because the three group tables
// carry a different number of fields per group.
make uc_find(tbl: list, cp: num, stride: num) -> num {
  hold n = len(tbl)
  hold lo = 0
  hold hi = u8_div(n, stride) - 1
  while lo <= hi {
    hold mid = u8_div(lo + hi, 2)
    hold a = tbl[mid * stride]
    hold b = tbl[mid * stride + 1]
    when cp < a {
      hi = mid - 1
    } otherwise {
      when cp > b {
        lo = mid + 1
      } otherwise {
        give mid
      }
    }
  }
  give 0 - 1
}

